# --- DISCOVERIES 10-24 (optional, no quest needs them): camp + note; BoatStranded + chest; hatch with a chest; buried treasure; viewpoint ---
place campfire_1 - at 23.2 -38.6 ground sit
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_SimpleTent - at 26.2 -36.6 ground sit yaw=137
place "Box Small" - at 21.2 -36.1 ground sit
place Note_Paper dnote at 21.2 -36.1 ground y=0.7 drop yaw=20
note dnote Castaway's note | DAY 40 - OR 41\n\nThe station people never came up for me. I watch their crane from here.\nAt night a light goes down the shaft and does not come back up.\nI have fish, rain, and this pencil. That is enough for now.
place BoatStranded dvan at -23.2 38.6 ground yaw=257
prop dvan tint.color=#6b5a48
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at -27.2 41.6 ground sit yaw=197
note dwreckchest Wreck's chest | A small chest from the wreck, its lid swollen shut by the salt: line, nails and scrap.
loot dwreckchest Rope*3;Nail*8;Scrap*3
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=38.6 z=23.2 r=4 seed=10991 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;Bolt*2
call treasure x=-38.6 z=-23.2 r=6 n=1 seed=10992
prop treasure10992 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;CopperOre*2
place Zone_Trigger dview at 7 44.4 ground
prop dview zone.id=sealkeeper_spire_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=The spire's lit windows stand over everything, and the cable from its winch runs down into the trench.

# --- Areas (10-24: every story island has places all over it and its quest crosses it): the storm ridge in the east, the keepers' cave in the
# north-west, the storm keeper's house in the south (its radio), the supply plane in the south-west
call sk_ridge x1=74 z1=-20 x2=80 z2=20 h=4 top=6 r=8
call sk_plants x=77 z=0 r=16 seed=10961
call sk_zone x=77 z=0 al=sk_ridge id=sk_ridge r=7 msg="The storm ridge. The Spire's switchboard windows flash with every gust; the zipline from here runs back down."
call sk_cave x=-46 z=30 h=3 yaw=180 al=sk_caverock chest=sk_cavechest
call sk_zone x=-46 z=25 al=sk_cave id=sk_cave r=4 msg="The keepers' cave: where the Spire's crew sat out the worst storms."
call sk_ruin x=0 z=-76 h=3 al=sk_ruin
call sk_ruin x=-12 z=-74 h=3 al=sk_ruin2
call sk_notebox x=2.5 z=-80.5 yaw=10 al=sk_ruinnote
call sk_plane x=-70 z=-30 h=3 yaw=60 al=sk_plane crate=sk_wreckcrate
call sk_notebox x=-75 z=-24.5 yaw=70 al=sk_wrecknote

# --- Tools in use (10-24: a tool or item given earlier in the storyline opens extras here, never the main path)
clear from 77 0 to 52 0 r=3
place ZiplinePath_Landmark skridgezip at 77 0 ground
zipto skridgezip 52 0
call vinecache x=56 z=56 r=8 seed=10971 chest=skvinechest vines=skvines items=Rope*3;Nail*8;TitaniumOre*1

# --- Unique layer (10-24): the storm keeper's radio: the generator by his house wants its part (in a toolbox near the
# keepers' cave); powered, the radio gives away the last supply drop
call powerradio x=6 z=-72 yaw=0 alias=skgen ralias=skradio rx=-0.75 rz=-76 rh=5 ryaw=0 cache=sksupply cx=40 cz=-62 cr=10 cseed=10981 items=Battery*2;CopperIngot*2;TitaniumIngot*1 kx=-58 kz=20 kr=8 seed=10982 toolbox=skbox

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Sealkeeper Spire
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Network's control spire in a storm over the trench: a generator, ziplines to the pump and door towers, fuses, a keypad - and two levers, RESTORE and SEAL. The ninth island of The Sunken Kingdom, the first half of its finale.
island on.arrive=message||A stone spire in the storm, a cable from its top running down into the sea.

story power|Base power on|Battery|You started the Spire's generator.
story pumped|Pumps primed|Hinge|You cranked the pump tower's valve: the Commons' pumps have pressure.
story fuse|Spire fuse|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A ceramic fuse from the door tower's lockers.
story fused|Fuse board set|Battery|You set the fuses: the spire's windows are lit.
story unlocked|Control room unlocked|Battery|You keyed the Commons' code into the control room's keypad.
story winched|Cable wound|Hinge|You wound the cable winch: the cable head is live.
story chosen|The choice made|Bolt|You pulled one of the two levers at the cable head.
story descended|Descend lever|Bolt|You pulled the descend lever.
story restorechoice|RESTORE pulled|Bolt|You chose RESTORE at the Sealkeeper Spire.
story sealchoice|SEAL pulled|Bolt|You chose SEAL at the Sealkeeper Spire.

note orders Sealkeeper's orders | SEALKEEPER'S ORDERS\n\n1. Power first: the generator on the base.\n2. Prime the pumps from the west tower. Fuses from the east tower.\n3. The control room is keyed with the Commons' code.\n4. Wind the cable. At the cable head: RESTORE, or SEAL. Not both. There is no both.\n5. Then go down. Somebody has to see it done.
note baselocker Base locker | The base locker: rope, a lamp and a crowbar.
note statusboard Network status board | NETWORK STATUS\n\nBiome Seven: GREEN (air)\nThalassa: SURFACE\nLumen Shelf: LIGHTS HALF\nCaisson Yard: IDLE\nHadal Commons: DOORS SHUT\nThe Hollow: - - - (no reading)
note pumplog Pump log | PUMP LOG\n\nPressure's held for nine years on one crank a week.\nThe week the doors were open, the pumps pulled something up the trench with the water.\nWe stopped cranking. Crank it now if you mean to RESTORE.
note warning Door warden's warning | DOOR WARDEN\n\nThree fuses, three lockers. Set them and the spire lights up - and everything down there sees it.\nIf you go to the Hollow, go when the lights are on. It hunts in the dark.
note networkmap The Network map | A map of the Pelagic Network: seven stations round a ring, three wavy lines across it - the Ringwave. At its centre, under the trench lip, one word: HOLLOW.
note inesmessage Ines's message | Ines's writing, quick and slanted:\n\nIf you freed me - thank you. If you didn't, someone left this for you anyway.\nRESTORE turns the Network back on. The lights, the pumps, the doors. It'll come up with them.\nSEAL drops the plug on the Hollow for good. The Commons will drown.\nI can't choose. You choose.
note twoswitches Two switches | Two levers on the cable head, under glass, labels stamped in brass:\n\nRESTORE - power to every station, the doors on the cycle.\nSEAL - the plug over the Hollow, the Network dark for good.\n\nPull one. The other dies with it.
note verdictrestore The verdict | RESTORE.\n\nAll down the cable, lights come on - station after station. Somewhere far below, great doors begin to move.\nPull the descend lever. Go down and see it through.
note verdictseal The verdict | SEAL.\n\nThe cable jerks. Far below, something heavy drops into place. The lights on the cable go out, one after another.\nPull the descend lever. Go down and see it through.
note fuselocker1 Deck fuse locker | A locker on the door tower's deck: a fuse.
note fuselocker2 Tower fuse locker | A locker inside the door tower: a fuse.
note fuselocker3 Shore fuse locker | A locker at the door tower's foot: a fuse.
loot baselocker Rope*3;Placeable_Lantern_Metal*1;Scrap*2
prop baselocker loot.refill=0
loot fuselocker1 story:fuse*1;Bolt*1
prop fuselocker1 loot.refill=0
loot fuselocker2 story:fuse*1;Scrap*1
prop fuselocker2 loot.refill=0
loot fuselocker3 story:fuse*1;Nail*5
prop fuselocker3 loot.refill=0

prop dockzone zone.id=dock
prop dockzone zone.radius=4
prop dockzone zone.message=The Spire's dock. A board with orders, nailed to a post.
prop screechers creature.count=4
prop screechers creature.respawn=0
prop generator obj.name=generator
prop generator beh.use=Start the generator
prop generator if.use=!signal|power
prop generator on.use=signal||power\ngive||story:power*1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The generator coughs, then roars. The base lights stutter on.
prop generator else.use=message||The generator is running.
prop pumpzone zone.id=pump_tower
prop pumpzone zone.radius=3
prop pumpzone zone.message=The pump tower. A crank on its deck.
prop pumpcrank obj.name=pumpcrank
prop pumpcrank beh.use=Turn the pump crank
prop pumpcrank if.use=!signal|pumped
prop pumpcrank on.use=signal||pumped\ngive||story:pumped*1\nmessage||The crank fights you, then turns. Far below, pumps thud awake.
prop pumpcrank else.use=message||The pumps have pressure.
prop doortowerzone zone.id=door_tower
prop doortowerzone zone.radius=3
prop doortowerzone zone.message=The door tower. A fuse board on the deck - empty.
prop fuseboard obj.name=fuseboard
prop fuseboard beh.use=Set the fuses
prop fuseboard if.use=has|story:fuse|3\n!signal|fused
prop fuseboard on.use=signal||fused\ngive||story:fused*1\nshow|spirelights\nmessage||Three fuses, three clunks. Across the water the spire's windows light up.
prop fuseboard else.use=message||The fuse board needs three fuses. The lockers in this tower hold them.
prop spirelights obj.name=spirelights
prop spirelights beh.hidden=1
prop stairzone zone.id=spire_stair
prop stairzone zone.radius=2.5
prop stairzone zone.message=The spire's door. A ladder inside goes up into the dark.
prop controlzone zone.id=control
prop controlzone zone.radius=3
prop controlzone zone.message=The control room. Lit windows, a map, a keypad, a winch.
prop controlpad obj.name=controlpad
prop controlpad beh.use=Key in the code
prop controlpad lock.code=2817
prop controlpad on.use=sound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nsignal||unlocked\ngive||story:unlocked*1\nmessage||The keypad blinks green. The winch's brake lets go.
prop controlpad else.use=message||The keypad wants the control room code. The Commons' council wrote it down.
prop winch obj.name=winch
prop winch beh.use=Wind the cable winch
prop winch if.use=signal|unlocked\n!signal|winched
prop winch on.use=signal||winched\ngive||story:winched*1\nshow|cable\nmessage||The winch grinds. Down at the shore the cable lifts out of the sea, dripping, live.
prop winch else.use=message||The winch is braked. The keypad releases it.
prop cable obj.name=cable
prop cable beh.hidden=1
prop cablezone zone.id=cable_head
prop cablezone zone.radius=3
prop cablezone zone.message=The cable head. Two levers under glass - and a third, by itself.
prop restore obj.name=restore
prop restore beh.use=Pull RESTORE
prop restore if.use=signal|winched\n!signal|chosen
prop restore on.use=signal||restore\nsignal||chosen\ngive||story:chosen*1\ngive||story:restorechoice*1\nshow|verdictrestore\nmessage||RESTORE. The lever slams home.
prop restore else.use=message||The lever won't move.
prop seal obj.name=seal
prop seal beh.use=Pull SEAL
prop seal if.use=signal|winched\n!signal|chosen
prop seal on.use=signal||seal\nsignal||chosen\ngive||story:chosen*1\ngive||story:sealchoice*1\nshow|verdictseal\nmessage||SEAL. The lever slams home.
prop seal else.use=message||The lever won't move.
prop verdictrestore obj.name=verdictrestore
prop verdictrestore beh.hidden=1
prop verdictseal obj.name=verdictseal
prop verdictseal beh.hidden=1
prop descend obj.name=descend
prop descend beh.use=Pull the descend lever
prop descend if.use=signal|chosen\n!signal|descend
prop descend on.use=signal||descend\ngive||story:descended*1\nmessage||The descend lever. Somewhere under the trench lip, a light comes on - the Hollow.
prop descend else.use=message||Not yet. RESTORE or SEAL first.
prop storm atmo.fog=#3a4048
prop storm atmo.fogAmount=0.5
prop storm atmo.light=#8a96a2
prop storm atmo.lightAmount=0.35
prop storm atmo.particles=mist
prop storm zone.radius=60

note sk_cavechest Keepers' chest | The keepers' storm chest: dry clothes gone to rags, a lamp, rope.
loot sk_cavechest Rope*3;Leather*2;Battery*1;Copper*2
prop sk_cavechest loot.refill=0
note sk_ruinnote Storm keeper's log | STORM KEEPER'S LOG\n\nThe radio on my table runs off the generator. The generator wants a part I lent to the cave crew.\nWith power, the radio tells you where the last supply drop came down.
note sk_wrecknote Supply pilot's log | SUPPLY PILOT'S LOG\n\nLast drop for the Spire. The storm took the plane; I kept the crate.\nThey are going to decide it soon - RESTORE or SEAL. I am not staying to see.
note sk_wreckcrate Supply plane crate | The supply plane's crate: what the Spire ordered, never delivered.
loot sk_wreckcrate MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*2;Plank*4
prop sk_wreckcrate loot.refill=0

quest title=The Choice
quest intro=The Spire on the Receiver - the Network's switchboard. Land at its dock.
step reach|dock|1|Land at the Spire's dock
step read|Sealkeeper's orders|1|Read the Sealkeeper's orders
step kill|Screecher|4|Drive off the screechers nesting on the spire
step open|Base locker|1|Open the base locker by the cable mast
step collect|story:power|1|Start the generator
step read|Network status board|1|Read the Network status board
step reach|pump_tower|1|Zipline from the cable mast to the pump tower
step collect|story:pumped|1|Turn the pump crank
step read|Pump log|1|Read the pump log
step reach|door_tower|1|Zipline from the cable mast to the door tower
step collect|story:fuse|3|Collect the three fuses from the door tower's lockers
step collect|story:fused|1|Set the fuses in the fuse board
step read|Door warden's warning|1|Read the door warden's warning
step reach|spire_stair|1|Go to the spire's door
step reach|control|1|Climb to the control room
step read|The Network map|1|Read the Network map
step collect|story:unlocked|1|Key in the control room code (the Commons' minutes had it)
step read|Ines's message|1|Read Ines's message on the desk
step collect|story:winched|1|Wind the cable winch
step reach|cable_head|1|Go down to the cable head on the shore
step read|Two switches|1|Read the two switches
step collect|story:chosen|1|Pull one: RESTORE or SEAL
step read|The verdict|1|Read the verdict
step reach|sk_ridge|1|Climb the storm ridge in the east
step reach|sk_cave|1|Find the keepers' cave in the north-west
step read|Storm keeper's log|1|Read the log in the storm keeper's house in the south
step read|Supply pilot's log|1|Read the log at the supply plane in the west
step collect|story:descended|1|Pull the descend lever
quest done=The choice is made. Under the trench lip the Hollow lights up - the Receiver finds it on band 500.
quest reward=TitaniumOre*2;Battery*2

save Sealkeeper Spire
